# Build output
bin/
obj/
.vs/
*.user

# npm
node_modules/
src/Shenora.React/dist/
src/Shenora.Cli/dist/
*.tgz

# Sample packaged frontend (built by `npm run build` in samples/Shenora.Sample.Web)
samples/Shenora.Sample.Desktop/wwwroot/

# Pack/publish output
publish/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# API-surface drift dumps (the .txt baselines ARE tracked)
*.actual

# Devtools scratch (family convention: _-prefixed, never OS temp)
devtools/_*
devtools/screenshots/
devtools/.cdp-port

# CI artifacts staged for packing. `Shenora.Launcher` packs the per-RID launcher binaries that
# the `launcher` workflow builds on two different runners; a release downloads them into this folder.
# They are BUILD OUTPUT from elsewhere — never sources, and never committed.
src/Shenora.Launcher/artifacts/

# Private local-only notes/config (real paths, sibling names, sensitive patterns) — never tracked
local/

# Subagent-driven-execution scratch: per-plan ledgers, task briefs, review packages. Working state
# for an in-flight plan, not a record — the record is the plan doc, the commits, and PROJECT_NOTES.
.superpowers/

# 🔴 Agent worktrees — a SECOND CHECKOUT of this repo, living inside it. Untracked until 2026-08-10,
# which meant one `git add -A` would have committed a whole duplicate tree, and every prose gate walked
# it as if it were ours: doc-drift went green → 114 failures, cite-scan 36 docs → 77, stale-scan 305
# occurrences → 594. Each hit named a real path in the WRONG COPY, so the repo reads as suddenly rotten
# and the obvious fix is to edit files that are about to be deleted. The scanners now skip any directory
# that is itself a checkout; this line is the other half, so the mistake cannot be committed either.
.claude/worktrees/
